WEBVTT

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:05.690
<i>The fact that there are those after Main 
and her strong mana has come to light.</i>

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:10.220
Main's mana is unbelievably great.

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:14.770
But if she can't control it, she is a 
danger to herself and those around her.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:19.270
If she is deemed dangerous,
 Main will be dealt with.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:23.000
<i>Meanwhile, a blue-robed priest 
she had never seen before</i>

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.570
<i>appeared before her as she gets ready 
to head to the Spring Prayer.</i>

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:29.970
Squeak "pwee" for me.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.870
Well? Go on! Squeak.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:36.370
Go on, go on.

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:39.130
Clearly, he has a terrible personality.

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:41.900
Just go ahead and humor him.

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:44.840
Pwee!

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:45.880
Excellent.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:47.630
Now, keep squeaking!

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:51.020
Pwee! Pwee! Pwee...

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:06.540
<b>Ascendance of a Bookworm</b>

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.050
<b>Ascendance of a Bookworm</b>

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:32.000
<b>Chapter Thirty
Spring Prayer</b>

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:33.490
Sylvester.

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:35.790
Come on, come on...

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:37.800
Main is weak. If you tease 
her too much, she will die.

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:44.190
What's this supposed to be?

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:45.930
Please give that back!

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:45.930
Whoa, there.

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:48.190
Give it back... please!

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:52.760
Come on... I asked you to give that back.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:57.280
That's the hair stick that Mom, 
Dad, and Tuuli made for me!

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:00.900
I hate guys like this!

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:05.690
Apprentice Priestess!

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:15.420
Hey, I was just teasing her a bit.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:17.640
You can get it back in 
your hair, can't you?

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:19.990
Yes. Thank you kindly.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:25.310
Go play with Damuel instead of Main. 
He won't break as easily.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:26.500
That's how Sylvester is with everyone. 
Don't let it get to you.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:26.510
Oh, fine.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:29.130
Want to play, Damuel?

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:31.500
Um, please, no!

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:35.840
Hm... This should do.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:37.770
Then let us go.

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:40.800
Damuel, pick Main up.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.700
Sylvester and Karstedt,
I need you to carry these.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:53.070
Sir Damuel, I'd like you to keep some 
distance from that blue-robed priest.

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:56.110
I wholeheartedly agree with you.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.750
Karstedt will lead.

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:05.270
Sylvester and I will be in the back, 
putting Main and Damuel in the middle.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:29.030
<i>That's Fran and the others 
who left earlier.</i>

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:31.700
<i>I wonder if we're going to the winter estate</i>

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:33.860
<i>that's in the farming village 
closest to the south gate.</i>

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:48.180
Move!

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:49.760
What the?!

00:04:58.760 --> 00:04:59.840
Wow!

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:08.030
So cool!

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:12.650
Is the Spring Prayer an event where priests 
show off various tricks for the farmers?

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:15.300
You don't need to learn anything from him.

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:19.610
We will now begin the Spring Prayer.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:21.720
Mayors, come forth.

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:37.140
Goddess of Water, who brings upon 
healing and change, Fruhtrane,

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:40.850
and the twelve kindred 
goddesses at her side...

00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:45.730
The God of Life, Ewigleben, 
has freed thine sister,

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:51.730
the Goddess of Earth, Geduldh. Now, 
aid her in bringing new life upon this land.

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:58.590
We offer you an invigorating song of joy.

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:01.070
We offer you our prayers and gratitude,

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:03.430
and ask for your pure protection in return.

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:09.680
May you bless all of the life 
upon this land with happiness.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.420
<i>It's green.</i>

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:21.960
We offer the Goddess of Earth, Geduldh, 
and the Goddess of Water, Fruhtrane,

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:23.470
our prayers and gratitude!

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:27.000
We offer the gods our prayers!

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.050
We offer the gods our prayers!

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:31.800
Thus ends the Spring Prayer.

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:36.720
Follow the will of the gods and live 
righteously along with the bounty of new life.

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:40.090
We offer you the gods' blessings.

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:58.100
Where are we?

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:00.840
This is Baron Blon's summer estate.

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:04.720
Nobles who have been put in charge of 
watching over farming villages by the lord

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:06.920
spend their time living in the 
estates in the farming villages

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:09.820
from the Spring Prayer to 
the Harvest Festival.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:14.490
<b>Taxes</b>

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:14.570
In the winter, they return to the nobles' 
district and give their yearly reports and taxes.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:19.210
So, going around to the farming villages 
and interacting with the farmers

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:21.120
during the Spring Prayer is very important.

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:27.610
That building there is where the nobles live,
 and the annex is where we priests will stay.

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:31.120
Arno should have already 
gone by to have it opened.

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:34.800
Welcome back.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:44.590
I would like to get dinner started, 
but there are only two dining halls.

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:46.200
What would you like to do?

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:50.100
We can all eat together in 
the larger dining hall.

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:54.730
Just make sure that Main and Sylvester 
are seated away from each other.

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:55.970
As you wish.

00:07:56.940 --> 00:08:00.960
All of you should get properly dressed 
and meet in the dining hall.

00:08:01.610 --> 00:08:04.650
Welcome back, Lady Main.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:07.100
First, let us get you changed.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:13.630
I feel alive again.

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.310
You look beautiful, Lady Main.

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:21.070
Thank you.

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:25.710
Hugo and Ella were working 
very hard on your meal.

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:26.810
Wait, why?

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:30.320
They didn't want to be 
outdone by another chef.

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:34.080
That just means I need to 
work harder, as well.

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:36.150
Ah...

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:40.550
Once you're properly dressed, you actually 
look no different than a noble lady.

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:43.170
You are far too kind, Lord Karstedt.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.410
You have become far more 
refined during the winter.

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:48.660
Thank you kindly.

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:51.930
Though I see that you still wear 
your heart on your sleeve.

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:57.630
You always give too much praise and 
critique at once, Head Priest!

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:00.660
Oh mighty King and Queen 
of the endless skies...

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:07.270
who doth grace us with thousands 
upon thousands of lives to consume,

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:11.650
O mighty Eternal Five who 
rule the mortal realm,

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:17.780
I offer thanks and prayers to thee, and do 
take part in the meal so graciously provided.

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:22.390
Mmm... This smells great.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:25.030
Why are you the only one 
with a different meal?

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:27.780
Fran, do you know?

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:30.210
Because someone else prepared your food.

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:32.790
Because I had someone else prepare my food.

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:35.950
They're using the smaller 
kitchen to prepare it.

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:41.130
My chef is extremely talented.

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:43.840
Wh-Why are you eating?!

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:45.650
Huh? What do you mean?

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:49.380
Sylvester was interested 
in your food, Main.

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:53.620
What? That's what he meant 
by it smells good?

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:55.790
How was I supposed to know that?

00:09:57.130 --> 00:09:59.240
I wouldn't mind giving you half.

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:01.690
H-Half?!

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:06.680
You can't possibly be suggesting that you 
wanted to take all of a poor commoner's meal...

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:11.650
Half will do just fine.

00:10:16.430 --> 00:10:19.340
Now, if you'll please excuse me.

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:22.630
Gentlemen, please enjoy 
the rest of your meal.

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:23.790
Main, wait.

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:27.670
Let us talk about trading chefs.

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:32.680
Lord Sylvester,

00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:36.200
they are chefs who we're borrowing 
from someplace else.

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:39.230
I cannot make any decisions 
regarding this trade.

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:41.420
Then I will negotiate with 
whoever they work for.

00:10:41.420 --> 00:10:42.200
Who is it?

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:46.940
Lord Sylvester, merchants 
can't say "no" to nobles.

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:49.230
That would end up being an order.

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:51.200
I see.

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:55.560
They are going to be the chefs of a 
restaurant that will be opening soon.

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:57.740
Ah, a restaurant?

00:10:57.740 --> 00:11:00.500
Preparing to open the restaurant and properly

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:03.350
training the chefs involves a lot
 of money and people.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:05.960
If you enjoyed their food,

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:09.340
please consider becoming a 
patron of that restaurant.

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:13.860
Very well. I'll do just that.

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:16.360
Thank you kindly.

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:18.600
<i>For the rest of the night,</i>

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:21.220
<i>we played the harspiel, and...</i>

00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:26.820
Since everyone is showcasing their 
talents, allow me to show you mine.

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:38.020
<i>...we also saw a sword dance. 
It was a very long night.</i>

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:42.340
That was cool, wasn't it? Now, praise me.

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:44.480
It was lovely...

00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:47.730
You didn't actually mean that. Try again.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:53.320
<i>I was forced to to praise him over again 
three times, and I became exhausted.</i>

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:57.900
<b>Ascendance of a
 Bookworm</b>

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:03.990
<b>Ascendance of a
 Bookworm</b>

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:06.710
<i>The next day, we handed 
over a small holy grail</i>

00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:08.880
<i>that we'd poured our mana into 
at the Dedication Ceremony.</i>

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:13.090
<i>After that, we went around to five 
different winter estates in a day.</i>

00:12:13.090 --> 00:12:17.500
<i>Then the next day, and the day after that, 
we continued to go to winter estates.</i>

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:22.010
We'll be going to see Viscount Gerlach next, 
but we'll be heading to him by carriage.

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:23.930
What? A carriage?

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:25.200
Let us regroup with the others.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:34.470
Main, use this to hide your face.

00:12:34.910 --> 00:12:38.800
Viscount Gerlach is quite interested in you.

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:43.500
He wanted you to stop by 
during the Spring Prayer.

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:46.740
He is very close with the high priest.

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:48.740
Be on your guard.

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:51.190
<i>So that's what he meant.</i>

00:12:54.010 --> 00:12:58.550
Ah, thank you for coming all 
this way, Lord Ferdinand.

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:02.770
Is that the apprentice priestess 
I've heard so much about?

00:13:03.570 --> 00:13:04.450
Yes.

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:06.630
You will be staying the night, won't you?

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:08.470
We will offer you nothing but the best.

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:13.760
No, we will be staying with 
Count Leisegang tonight.

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:15.640
I see.

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:18.270
That's too bad.

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:27.470
Head Priest...

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:31.590
I don't think I'm feeling very well.

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:35.130
Then you should go to bed early tonight.

00:13:35.130 --> 00:13:38.130
I will leave the medicine 
I have prepared with Fran.

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:40.700
Thank you kindly.

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:47.940
<i>This is an attendant's 
room, but it's very comfy.</i>

00:14:10.100 --> 00:14:13.600
I slept so well! I feel all better!

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:17.350
Good morning, Lady Main.

00:14:17.350 --> 00:14:20.290
This may seem sudden, but the head 
priest would like to see you.

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:33.210
Bandits entered here late last night.

00:14:33.210 --> 00:14:36.190
Bandits... You mean thieves?

00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:40.290
Not quite. We believe they 
wanted to kidnap you.

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:43.860
Two men snuck into my room last night.

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:47.020
<i>I see. Of course, they wouldn't think 
the person they're trying to kidnap</i>

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:49.730
<i>would be in an attendant's room.</i>

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:54.110
I tried to catch them as 
soon as I saw them, but...

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:56.400
Did they get away?

00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:57.360
No.

00:14:57.690 --> 00:15:01.240
I caught one, let Lord Ferdinand handle him,

00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:03.250
then I went after the other one.

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:06.130
He managed to get on a horse and flee.

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:08.770
I was about to pursue him with my highbeast,

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:12.270
but then he and the horse exploded.

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:21.630
The one we captured took his own 
life as Ferdinand was disarming him.

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:23.380
No...

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:26.810
We considered not telling 
you about this incident,

00:15:26.810 --> 00:15:30.290
but we decided it'd be best 
if you knew what was going on

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:32.100
since they're after you.

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:34.920
I'm quite certain that Viscount 
Gerlach is behind this.

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:37.150
Be careful, Main.

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:42.150
There's no chance that the culprit 
is actually Count Leisegang?

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:45.800
No. This is my mother's family home.

00:15:46.330 --> 00:15:50.400
They wouldn't dare try to 
harm someone in my company.

00:15:56.210 --> 00:15:59.760
<i>I ate my breakfast, though it 
went down with difficulty,</i>

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:02.280
<i>and finished my morning and evening duties.</i>

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:08.360
Now, let us regroup with the carriage.

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:10.850
<i>It's finally over.</i>

00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:13.870
An attack!

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:16.180
We will go first.

00:16:17.650 --> 00:16:20.810
Sir Damuel, let's hurry, as well!

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:23.820
I cannot catch up to 
their speed with my mana.

00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:27.050
Then go ahead and use my mana, too!

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:30.450
Thank you!

00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:53.250
What is that black thing?

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:55.160
That is a God of Darkness barrier.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.550
Mana-based attacks won't work against it.

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:01.360
One of the attackers must be a noble!

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:08.480
Head Priest! If mana won't 
work against the carriage,

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:11.620
please use magic to blast those men away!

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:15.080
Wait! They might just 
be men from this domain.

00:17:15.320 --> 00:17:17.850
Fran and Rosina are more important!

00:17:17.850 --> 00:17:20.830
If I pray to the gods, 
I can use magic, can't I?

00:17:21.950 --> 00:17:23.580
Stop her at once!

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:24.490
I cannot.

00:17:24.490 --> 00:17:25.470
What do you mean?!

00:17:25.470 --> 00:17:28.360
But I can at least give her some direction.

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:30.870
Main! Pray to the wind!

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:44.800
Goddess of Wind that rules 
over protection, Schutzaria,

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:48.080
and the twelve kindred 
goddesses at her side...

00:17:48.390 --> 00:17:54.090
Main, keep going so that the God of Darkness 
barrier continues to devour your mana.

00:17:54.430 --> 00:17:59.040
Hear my prayer and grant me holy power!

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:03.570
Grant me a shield of wind that will 
ward away those who wish to do us harm!

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:15.050
What the?!

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:19.940
Well done.

00:18:19.940 --> 00:18:21.100
I know, right?!

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:23.820
Way to go, shield formed by the power 
of the Goddess of Wind, Schutzaria!

00:18:27.820 --> 00:18:30.880
I sensed some mana from the forest just now!

00:18:31.150 --> 00:18:33.510
We will go investigate the forest.

00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:36.370
Damuel, continue protecting Main in the air.

00:18:36.370 --> 00:18:37.100
Yes, sir!

00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:37.840
No!

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:38.860
Huh?

00:18:48.750 --> 00:18:50.140
Ferdinand!

00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:51.480
Take this!

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:56.150
That was so scary...

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:57.230
Of course, he <i>would</i> do that.

00:18:57.580 --> 00:18:59.580
You stay here, Ferdinand.

00:18:59.580 --> 00:19:01.970
We might be dealing with 
the decoy over there.

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:02.870
Understood.

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:03.960
Come, Karstedt!

00:19:03.960 --> 00:19:04.230
Yes, sir!

00:19:06.190 --> 00:19:11.010
What he did may seem violent,
but we are prioritizing your safety.

00:19:11.010 --> 00:19:11.790
Huh?

00:19:12.800 --> 00:19:16.380
Main, will you pray with me that 
they are successful in battle?

00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:25.350
May the God of War Angriff, kindred of the 
God of Fire, Leidenschaft, protect them.

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:33.570
It looks like a phoenix.

00:19:56.570 --> 00:19:58.300
Such power.

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:00.710
The carriage! Is the carriage safe?!

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:03.190
It's perfectly fine.

00:20:03.190 --> 00:20:04.710
Oh, thank goodness.

00:20:06.310 --> 00:20:07.870
What's the matter, Main?

00:20:07.870 --> 00:20:10.930
Head Priest, I'm out of mana.

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:12.690
You're out of mana?

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:22.580
Lady Main, are you awake?

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:24.060
Rosina...

00:20:24.060 --> 00:20:26.250
You mustn't move too suddenly.

00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:28.890
You must have pushed yourself rather hard.

00:20:28.890 --> 00:20:30.440
Is everyone okay?

00:20:30.440 --> 00:20:32.190
Yes. Everyone is fine.

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:34.010
Thank goodness...

00:20:37.810 --> 00:20:42.580
<i>By the time I woke up again, the head 
priest had brought me my medicine.</i>

00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:44.960
Drink this.

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:48.550
<i>He said he'd work on the flavor,</i>

00:20:48.550 --> 00:20:50.770
<i>but it was still absolutely awful.</i>

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:57.120
From what I heard later, apparently they 
didn't know who set up the dark barrier.

00:20:57.480 --> 00:21:02.510
Mostly because Lord Karstedt's attack 
turned everything in the area to dust.

00:21:03.230 --> 00:21:06.800
Was that because of our prayers?

00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:07.980
It may be.

00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:10.750
Keep quiet until you're spoken to.

00:21:11.400 --> 00:21:13.170
Okay...

00:22:47.050 --> 00:22:50.050
<b>Next Chapter
The Gift from the Blue-Robed
 Priest and Going Home</b>

00:22:50.290 --> 00:22:53.780
You do far too many things 
that put you in danger.

00:22:54.140 --> 00:22:58.260
You had magical items with you this time, 
so when we offered our prayers to the gods,

00:22:58.260 --> 00:23:00.060
a spell activated.

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:01.800
If you had lacked magical items,

00:23:01.800 --> 00:23:03.670
your mana would've lost control 
and you would've died.

00:23:03.670 --> 00:23:04.920
What?!

00:23:04.920 --> 00:23:07.860
Wait, didn't we do this all before?

00:23:07.860 --> 00:23:09.070
I'll say it as many times as needed.

00:23:09.400 --> 00:23:13.540
If your mana leaks out of your body
 until it begins to flow out all at once,

00:23:13.540 --> 00:23:16.830
your body, the vessel, cannot sustain itself.

00:23:16.830 --> 00:23:19.080
Your skin will start to bubble,

00:23:19.080 --> 00:23:21.480
much like when you boil water.

00:23:21.480 --> 00:23:25.850
Once your skin can no longer hold it 
in, it'll burst, and your flesh—

00:23:26.690 --> 00:23:29.000
I can't hear you! I don't want to hear it!

00:23:30.290 --> 00:23:32.490
Hey! I wasn't done talking!

00:23:31.630 --> 00:23:34.660
I'm sorry! I'll never do it again!

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.010
Illustration by: Gilse
